[38;2;124;124;124mFirst, let me recall the definitions and key facts.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m$\mathcal{E}(\mathbb{R}) = C^\infty(\mathbb{R})$ with its standard Fréchet [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtopology (uniform convergence of all derivatives on compact sets).[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m$\mathcal{E}'(\mathbb{R})$ is the dual, consisting of compactly supported [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mdistributions.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe weak topology $\sigma(\mathcal{E}', \mathcal{E})$ on $\mathcal{E}'$ is the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtopology of pointwise convergence on elements of $\mathcal{E}$, i.e., $T_n \to [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mT$ weakly iff $\langle T_n, \varphi \rangle \to \langle T, \varphi \rangle$ for [0m[38;2;124;124;124mall $\varphi \in \mathcal{E}$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mThe strong dual topology $\beta(\mathcal{E}', \mathcal{E})$ on $\mathcal{E}'$ is[0m[38;2;124;124;124mthe topology of uniform convergence on bounded subsets of $\mathcal{E}$. A [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mneighborhood base at 0 is given by polars of bounded sets: $B^\circ = \{T \in [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\mathcal{E}' : \sup_{\varphi \in B} |\langle T, \varphi \rangle| \leq 1\}$ for [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mbounded $B \subset \mathcal{E}$.[0m

